1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:03,420
Exponents and powers. A short way to write repeated

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:08,283
multiplication: base, exponent and power. Let us see why

3
00:00:08,283 --> 00:00:09,131
we need it.

4
00:00:09,687 --> 00:00:13,227
Start with a simple product: three times three times

5
00:00:13,227 --> 00:00:17,127
three. Now keep going, up to six factors of

6
00:00:17,127 --> 00:00:19,987
three. Every single three has to be written out.

7
00:00:19,987 --> 00:00:23,281
Do we really need to write three six times?

8
00:00:23,281 --> 00:00:25,598
There must be a shorter way.

9
00:00:26,193 --> 00:00:29,187
Let us count them. Three times three times three

10
00:00:29,187 --> 00:00:32,673
times three times three times three: six equal factors.

11
00:00:32,673 --> 00:00:36,507
That small raised number tells us how many times

12
00:00:36,507 --> 00:00:39,790
the base is used as a factor. So three

13
00:00:39,790 --> 00:00:44,104
to the power six means six threes multiplied together.

14
00:00:44,747 --> 00:00:47,664
Look closely at three to the power six. The

15
00:00:47,664 --> 00:00:49,987
large number at the bottom is the base: three,

16
00:00:49,987 --> 00:00:53,809
the number that is multiplied again and again. The

17
00:00:53,809 --> 00:00:58,127
small raised number is the exponent: six, the number

18
00:00:58,127 --> 00:01:01,809
of factors. The whole expression is called a power.

19
00:01:01,809 --> 00:01:04,638
We read it as three raised to the power six.

20
00:01:05,260 --> 00:01:08,080
Now send five factors of four through the power

21
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:11,791
compressor. In they go: four times four times four

22
00:01:11,791 --> 00:01:14,915
times four times four. The machine counts five factors

23
00:01:14,915 --> 00:01:19,380
and writes four to the power five. Send it

24
00:01:19,380 --> 00:01:22,155
back the other way, and four to the power

25
00:01:22,155 --> 00:01:25,251
five expands into five fours multiplied.

26
00:01:25,910 --> 00:01:28,710
Here is a mistake to avoid. Four to the

27
00:01:28,710 --> 00:01:30,983
power five is not four times five. Four to

28
00:01:30,983 --> 00:01:34,257
the power five means five fours multiplied, which is

29
00:01:34,257 --> 00:01:37,790
one thousand and twenty four. Four times five is

30
00:01:37,790 --> 00:01:42,480
only twenty. The exponent counts factors, not how many

31
00:01:42,480 --> 00:01:44,081
times to multiply.

32
00:01:44,784 --> 00:01:47,864
Powers of ten are the most useful of all.

33
00:01:47,864 --> 00:01:50,457
Ten to the power one is ten, and ten

34
00:01:50,457 --> 00:01:54,156
squared is ten times ten: one hundred. Ten cubed

35
00:01:54,156 --> 00:01:57,246
is one thousand. Every new factor of ten adds

36
00:01:57,246 --> 00:02:00,224
another zero. Ten to the power nine is a

37
00:02:00,224 --> 00:02:03,695
one followed by nine zeros: one thousand million.

38
00:02:04,337 --> 00:02:06,192
Now the reason we need all this. The Sun

39
00:02:06,192 --> 00:02:10,017
is about fourteen crore metres across: a one and

40
00:02:10,017 --> 00:02:13,504
a four, followed by eight zeros. In exponential form

41
00:02:13,504 --> 00:02:16,269
that is one point four times ten to the

42
00:02:16,269 --> 00:02:20,129
power nine. The same short line writes the distance

43
00:02:20,129 --> 00:02:22,828
to the Sun, or the age of the universe.

44
00:02:23,323 --> 00:02:26,659
Numbers can also grow very fast. One grain on

45
00:02:26,659 --> 00:02:29,243
the first square of a chessboard, two on the

46
00:02:29,243 --> 00:02:32,523
next, four on the next, then eight, sixteen, thirty

47
00:02:32,523 --> 00:02:35,999
two. Every square doubles the one before it. By

48
00:02:35,999 --> 00:02:39,371
the last square the number is enormous, and only

49
00:02:39,371 --> 00:02:42,614
exponents can write it comfortably.

50
00:02:43,289 --> 00:02:47,307
Your turn. Three questions. Write seven times seven times

51
00:02:47,307 --> 00:02:52,569
seven times seven in exponential form. Expand two to

52
00:02:52,569 --> 00:02:56,385
the power five. Name the base and the exponent

53
00:02:56,385 --> 00:02:58,000
in ten to the power six.

54
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:11,887
Seven is repeated four times, so that is seven

55
00:03:11,887 --> 00:03:14,894
to the power four. Two to the power five

56
00:03:14,894 --> 00:03:18,435
is five twos multiplied together. And in ten to

57
00:03:18,435 --> 00:03:21,660
the power six, ten is the base and six

58
00:03:21,660 --> 00:03:23,491
is the exponent.

59
00:03:24,014 --> 00:03:26,382
One last look. The base is the number that

60
00:03:26,382 --> 00:03:29,784
repeats. The exponent counts how many times it is

61
00:03:29,784 --> 00:03:33,854
used as a factor. The power is the compact

62
00:03:33,854 --> 00:03:38,039
expression that writes it in one place. Remember: exponents

63
00:03:38,039 --> 00:03:41,824
make repeated multiplication short. Thank you for watching, and

64
00:03:41,824 --> 00:03:43,305
see you in the next lesson.
